Baobap City game design document

Ad Text:
Baobap city, a city on a out of business offshore plattform west of the Saloum delta and the Gambia river. 
Inhabitat by the former workers and many more climate crisis refugees, expanded by adding additional oil rigs and pontoons. 
A new center of business and opportunities due to new international climate crisis laws and regulations. Your target destination to score a big corporate deal. 
Your deal may change the life of the people here, but exploring the city could also change your deal in a even more beneficial way...

Genre and features:
Interactive text only story in a near future climate crisis setting. 

Audience:
People who want to enjoy a interactive story where choices can change the ending.

Selling Point:
Decisions matter, short story, contemporary theme, exotic place

Player experience and interface:
Explore a living city by freely choosing, where to go and what do / see.
Not everything can be experienced in one playthrough.
Events and choices can alter your options on your business deal.

Game mechanic and interactivity:
Choices, optional lore at certain places (marked as interactive choice), Day cycle, missable events, multiple endings, random events

Visual and audio style:
Text only, general map available on major places, no audio?

Platform and tech stack:
Inkle for the main game, draw.io for map

